##  Conclusions between cluster 1, 12 and 14

Cluster 1 and 14 present very similar genetic composition particularly within their predominant set of Myelin score.

Even though cluster 12 presents a fairly similar Myelin score within the MBP predominant spots of this tissue, this cluster demonstrates a shift towards lower genetic expression of genes that present higher SCT transformed RNA expression within cluster 1 and 14. 

Interestingly a majority of cells within cluster 12 are actively expression KIF5A a marker that has previously been associated to correlate negatively with tumour grade, with lower levels of expression being highly present in GBM tumour cells (Joyce & Lindsay, 2024).

This could be a good explanation on why these clusters present such high similarity but also, somewhat dissimilar, with a high chance of a GBM tumour slowly forming within cluster 1 and 14, while cluster 12 cells demonstrate to be closely within healthy states.

Another major factor that may indicate this is the highly expression of CD14 and CD163 cells within cluster 1 and 14, indicating direct activity of immune system in this region and possibly part of a forming GBM. 

# Final Conclusions

## Clusters 5 and 9 driving cluster 7 hypoxia and newly formed GBM.

With Clusters 5 and 9 being directly associated to fibrotic areas rich in collagen, this region may be directly correlated with a GBM formation in late necrotic stages, already forming collagen-rich repairing tissue. 

Cluster 7 demonstrates particularly high expression of Hypoxic and Metastic genes, revealing a new area of metastasis forming within the region. 

## Clusters 1 and 14 Vs 12 (MBP)

Cluster 1 and 14 may represent a new cancer formation within the myelin rich areas of the brain, and even though distant from the main region of this tumour, this may be happening due to the metastatic nature of GBM. 

Cluster 12 on the other hand, demonstrates particularly healthy levels when compared to the other two myelin rich clusters, mediated by lower levels of immune cell associated RNA expression, coupled with highly expressed KIF5A marker, which had a negative correlation to tumour grade.

